Hello,

maybe someone is interested in the following information: It's possible t=
o=20
use a Matrox G450 DH PCI on the DEC Avati platform. I was successful in=20
getting one of these cards to run in my Alphastation 200 4/166. Be sure t=
o=20
use the latest SRM firmware (v7.0-9). The SRM bios emulation is not able =
to=20
use the Matrox with the original Matrox bios (I've tried v1.3 and v1.4=20
without success). The trick is to update the G450 to the v2.00-36 firmwar=
e=20
which is provided by IBM for it's Intellistation series. Just search on=20
IBM's support site with the keyword G450 and you will find an entry which=
 is=20
called QE3T03A. The update process requires that the G450 is used in an=20
normal x86-PC. After updating the bios you can use the G450 with the=20
Alphastation. Be patient: It takes up to 5 seconds until the bootup scree=
n=20
appears. On debian you also have to compile the Kernel for G400/G450 supp=
ort=20
if you want to use the framebuffer.
BTW, if you've got an old Avanti Alphastation and want to upgrade the=20
memory, the Kingston KTV-Z6000/512 is a good choice. I've upgraded my Alp=
ha=20
with this kit to 384 MB. 36-bit PS/2 RAM is hard to find.
I've made the experience that an original Mylex DAC960PD-3 RAID controlle=
r=20
runs great in the Avanti Alphastation when the latest DEC firmware for KZ=
PSC=20
(release v2.70) is flashed. I've used an external flash device to program=
=20
the Intel flash chip. It's possible to configure the RAID configuration w=
ith=20
the DEC utility (you have to use ARC to start the program) and to boot fr=
om=20
the RAID array out of SRM. The DEC firmware also supports SCSI harddisks=20
manufactured from other brands (IBM for example).
I hope that someone can use this information.

Regards, Eike=20



